WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.509
Speaker 1: OK, I have a couple sort of like
Keeping Them Honest type stories for you today.

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:12.059
We have been covering these scams, grifts
and crony con jobs that have been many of

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:15.759
the contracts given out during the Trump administration.

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:21.140
And that includes the company that it was
only around for two months with no employees.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:26.980
That was given a massive contract to be basically
a middleman for PPY back in twenty twenty.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.690
Earlier this week, we talked about API JECT.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.960
The company given a one point three dollars
billion combination of contracts and loan

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.630
loans to make vaccine syringes were about
200 million doses in.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.160
They haven't even built the factory.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.660
They've got not a single vaccine syringe out
there.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.450
And this next story is actually about some
of these so-called deals that Donald Trump

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.630
made back in 2016 and 2017.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:56.170
And even before being inaugurated in 2016,
he announced one or two and then made some

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.600
in 2017.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:04.589
You might remember that Donald Trump once
bragged about a supposed ten billion dollar

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:12.179
deal and factory in Wisconsin that he, I guess,
convinced the company Foxconn to make.

00:01:12.179 --> 00:01:17.310
He once referred to this deal as the, quote,
eighth wonder of the of the world.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.759
And there was really big fanfare about it
at the White House in July of 2017.

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:26.100
Trump saying it's ten billion dollars, it's
13000 jobs.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:32.220
It's an incredible example of how I'm doing
my America first thing of manufacturing coming

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.270
back to the United States.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.909
And it was all going to be incredible.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:40.549
It would be a factory for cutting edge flat
panel televisions and monitors, and it would

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:43.249
make Wisconsin a destination for tech firms.

00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:44.960
And it was all going to be just great.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:48.509
But some of us were suspicious for a couple
of different reasons.

00:01:48.509 --> 00:01:54.359
Number one, Foxconn is a supply company with
a very charismatic founder and then chairman

00:01:54.359 --> 00:01:58.630
Terry Gou, who is very PR thirsty.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:02.200
And a lot of it seemed like it was mostly
about public relations.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:07.560
And we were also skeptical of these deals
that are really just, hey, take some money

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.209
and do me a favor rather than economic policy.

00:02:11.209 --> 00:02:17.569
And indeed, there were reports that even executives
at Foxconn at the time were skeptical that

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:23.700
this was ever going to happen, not the least
of which was because the suppliers for the

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.810
LCD panels they were supposedly going to make
were nowhere near Wisconsin.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.150
And it made very little sense to actually
manufacture those there.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.310
Case in point, the project never started as
described.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:42.250
And now Foxconn is announcing, you know, four
years later, now we're going to scale back

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.299
what that project is going to be.

00:02:44.299 --> 00:02:48.430
And instead of ten billion dollars, Foxconn
has announced it will be six hundred and seventy

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:55.450
two million, not nothing, but that's a 93
percent reduction in the dollar value of the

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.450
project.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.159
Trump also bragged it would bring 13000 jobs
to Wisconsin.

00:03:00.159 --> 00:03:02.849
Foxconn now says, well, it's not going to
be 13000.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:08.170
It's going to be fourteen hundred and fifty
four, which is an 89 nine percent reduction

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.349
in the number of jobs that were promised and
that Donald Trump Trump announced.

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:15.390
So should this surprise us know?

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:17.430
But there's another aspect to this.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:22.170
I said at the time when Donald Trump and Mike
Pence were doing their victory tours, announcing,

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:27.499
oh, Foxconn is coming to Wisconsin and carrier
air conditioner is staying in.

00:03:27.499 --> 00:03:29.950
I think it was Indiana.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.909
I pointed out at the time, even if true.

00:03:32.909 --> 00:03:35.900
And of course, with many of these deals, as
we're now seeing, it wasn't true.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.290
But even if true, those deals were not economic
policy.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.340
They were not scalable.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:48.090
They were Trump giving specific companies
a bunch of cash, often in the form of tax

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:53.290
breaks or loans that sometimes don't even
need to be repaid to do a specific thing that

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.209
might not even be dictated by the market.

00:03:55.209 --> 00:03:59.569
Like, for example, Foxconn making LCD panels
in a place that's really far from where they

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:00.750
got all of their parts.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:07.739
And at the time, the Foxconn deal was denounced
by many in Wisconsin who were rightly saying

00:04:07.739 --> 00:04:10.629
this is a tax giveaway to a foreign company.

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:13.849
They're getting they're getting tax breaks.

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:15.799
They're are getting water rights.

00:04:15.799 --> 00:04:22.470
They're getting the green light to acquire
and demolish houses via eminent domain to

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.700
build their factory.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:24.760
It's not economic policy.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:25.760
You can't scale this.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.900
It's just a handout.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:32.190
Trump bought the deal with our tax money,
and that's exactly what this is becoming.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:37.030
Now, Foxconn did start buying houses to demolish
for their factory.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:42.030
They are going to do it eventually, but it
will be 90 percent smaller than was promised.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:46.620
And in fact, they're not even going to be
building a factory.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:50.140
For the flat panel displays, that detail has
also changed.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:55.140
They're going to be making server components
and communications technology products and

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.730
maybe medical devices, which is fine, but
every detail fell apart from the original

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:04.040
deal, and it will be 10 percent of what it
was promised to be five, six years later.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.040
Who even knows when?

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:09.540
So the project is another microcosm of the
Trump presidency.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.540
In sum, total.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.590
And it wasn't just Trump taking his victory
laps with this project.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:20.240
Then Republican Governor Scott Walker and
the Wisconsin Republican Party at the time

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.040
were also loudly bragging and boasting about
this.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:30.560
And it is because it has become absolutely
it's become pennies on the dollar what it

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:35.830
was supposed to be riding on our tax money,
an important detail

